:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=DSPSBSD.Display Subsystem Description - Help
:P.What a subsystem description holds: its attributes, its storage
pools and the entries that decide which jobs it starts and how it
routes them. Type an option number and press Enter.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBS'.Subsystem description
:P.The subsystem description, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STATUS'.Status
:P.The status shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT1'.Operational attributes
:P.Option 1. Operational attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT2'.Pool definitions
:P.Option 2. Pool definitions.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT3'.Autostart job entries
:P.Option 3. Autostart job entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT4'.Work station name entries
:P.Option 4. Work station name entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT5'.Work station type entries
:P.Option 5. Work station type entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT6'.Job queue entries
:P.Option 6. Job queue entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT7'.Routing entries
:P.Option 7. Routing entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT8'.Communications entries
:P.Option 8. Communications entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT9'.Remote location name entries
:P.Option 9. Remote location name entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT10'.Prestart job entries
:P.Option 10. Prestart job entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT20'.Every entry, one display after another
:P.Option 20. Every entry, one display after another.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSBSD/OPT21'.Work with the subsystem's jobs
:P.Option 21. Work with the subsystem's jobs.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DSPKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBSLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MAXJOBS'.Maximum jobs in subsystem
:P.The maximum jobs in subsystem shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SGNDSPF'.Sign-on display file
:P.The sign-on display file shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SGNLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SYSLIBLE'.System library list entry
:P.The system library list entry shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ASPGRP'.Auxiliary storage pool group
:P.The auxiliary storage pool group shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WLGRP'.Workload group
:P.The workload group shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/POOLID'.Pool ID
:P.The pool ID of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/POOLSIZE'.Storage Size (M)
:P.The storage Size (M) of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ACTLVL'.Activity Level
:P.The activity Level of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/AJEJOB'.Job
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/AJEJOBD'.Job Description
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/AJELIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DTLKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F9=Display all detailed descriptions
:PD.Display all detailed descriptions.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WSNES/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WSNAME'.Name
:P.The name of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WSJOBD'.Job Description
:P.The job description that supplies the job's attributes, by name and
library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WSJOBDL'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WSMAX'.Max Active
:P.The max Active of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WSNES/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display work station name details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display work station name
details it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WSTES/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WSTES/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display work station type details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display work station type
details it.
:EPARML.
